# Generated files from regression tests
*/backend
*/backend.zig
*/backend.err
*/compile_backend.err
*/compile_kz.err
*/compile_intermediate.err
*/compile_zig.err
*/intermediate
*/intermediate.zig
*/output
*/output.zig
*/output_emitted
*/output_emitted.zig
*/actual.txt
*/a.out

# Ignore all files without extensions (likely binaries)
*

# Keep directories (at any depth)
!*/

# Keep source and expected files (at any depth)
!**/*.kz
!**/*.k
!**/*.kjs
!**/*.kcs
!**/*.kc
!**/*.kgpu
!**/expected.txt
!**/expected_output.txt
!**/expected_error.txt
!**/expected_patterns.txt
!**/expected.transcript
!**/expected_comptime.txt
!**/expected.json
!**/EXPECT
!**/EXPECT_TIMEOUT
!**/EXPECT_TRAP
!**/COMPILE_ONLY
!**/SKIP
!**/MUST_*
!**/SHOULD_*
!**/PARSER_TEST
!**/LANGUAGES
!**/JS_REFUSES
!**/CS_REFUSES
!**/C_REFUSES
!**/WITNESS_CHECK
!**/ALIVE2_CHECK
!**/FLOW_EVAL_CHECK
!**/C_REFINE_CHECK
!**/HOLDS_CHECK
!**/CLAIMS_CHECK
!**/STRIP_AST_CHECK
!**/CLAIMS_AST_CHECK
!**/ARGS
!**/STDIN
!**/input.txt
!**/*.data

# Keep file-source template fixtures (620_008/620_009 read a template at
# compile time; the fixture is the test's content every bit as much as input.k)
!**/banner.txt
!**/hello.txt

# Keep bundle fixtures — .icns is the app-icon input the bundle tests carry
# (908_); binary, but the test IS the bytes it packages.
!**/*.icns

# Keep suite profiles — named test selections, one glob per line
!profiles/*.txt

# Nested .gitignore files are deliberate (nbody/, local fixture rules)
!**/.gitignore

# Keep documentation and marker files (at any depth)
!**/README.md
!**/*.md
!**/.MARKER
!**/TODO
!**/RULING
!**/NEEDS_RULING
!**/PRIORITY
!**/BENCHMARK
!**/BROKEN
!**/BUG_*
!**/THRESHOLD

# Keep scripts (at any depth)
!**/post.sh
!**/*.sh

# Keep baseline files for performance tests (at any depth)
!**/baseline.zig
!**/fixture.zig
!**/baseline.go
!**/*.go
!**/baseline.rs
!**/Cargo.toml
!**/COMPILER_FLAGS
!**/*.c
!**/koru.json

# Keep benchmark comparison files
!**/*.py
!**/*.lua

# Keep language-shootout translations (mojo-comparison/*.mojo are the fixture —
# the verdict files quote compiler output over exactly these sources)
!**/*.mojo

# Keep vendored fixtures and their pins (std/vendor tests). A vendored tree is
# checked-in third-party source — it IS the fixture, and its contents are what
# the pin is taken over, so every byte has to survive a fresh clone. Scoped to
# `vendored/` so the blanket `*.zig` artifact ignore above still holds elsewhere.
!**/vendored/**
!**/vendor.lock

# Keep mounted-scope module sources (440_056 and successors). A `module/` dir
# is the checked-in .dylib source the test compiles and mounts at runtime —
# the fixture, not emitted output. Scoped to `module/` for the same reason
# `vendored/` is.
!**/module/*.zig

# Generated .app bundles (must come last — !*/ above would otherwise
# un-ignore the directory and let git descend into it)
*.app
